      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Everyday calls and local records in Independent Mode do not need it. Connect a service when you need MCP, an external backend, cloud backups, or scheduled calls.\nDeploy in your own Supabase project, run a connector on your computer or server, or connect a Tincall-compatible backend. MCP, backups, and calls can share a service and be enabled according to its capabilities. No separate deployments are needed. Contacts can share a URL, but each contact’s MCP configuration belongs in the corresponding AI’s MCP settings.\nBackground calls also need device binding, push-capable app signing, and a matching push service. Scheduled Independent Mode calls need a schedule. A successful deployment or connection alone does not finish background call setup."
          }
        }
      }
